<title>POLAND: POLAND'S GORZOW TO HOLD MUNI BOND TENDER DEC 17.</title>
<headline>POLAND'S GORZOW TO HOLD MUNI BOND TENDER DEC 17.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's western city of Gorzow Wielkopolski will hold a 20 million zloty municipal bond tender on December 17, the Nowa Europa daily reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Gorzow's issue will be divided into two 10 million zloty tranches, which will have maturities of three and four years.</p>
<p>The city plans to invest the money in modernising roads.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
